msgid "<center><b>WITH SPECIAL MATINÉES AT<br/>CHICAGO - Aug. 29 | ST. LOUIS - Sept. 2<br/>DENVER - Sept. 5 | LOS ANGELES - Sept. 9<br/>DON'T MISS YOUR CHANCE!</b></center>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You couldn't have found a better roadmap if you planned it. There's no way to confirm if this schedule still holds true after the events last night, but from what little you know of Sylvester Blake, he's not the type to do anything halfway, nor keep an audience waiting.\n"
"Plans form and crumble in your head as you return to your home, but nothing has cemented by the time you arrive. You enter to find Thea at your kitchen table, studying Blake's tome carefully. She nearly jumps with surprise, but gives a relieved smile at the sight of you. Mercy... I keep expecting something horrible after all those months Thea gestures to a telegram on the table that arrived while you were out -from Minnie Klein, your newspaper contact.\n"
"You've barely picked up the message when a knock sounds firmly at the door; startling both you and Thea. You open it cautiously, but find a broad man in dark blue work clothes with his cap in hand, with a young lady in similar clothes beside him. \"I um.... hope this is a good time,\" he says with clear lack of practice with polite conversation. \"You don't know me, but my boy told me that you saved his life after he snuck off to the circus last night. I'm Ralph Dykstra, engineer with the Old Colony Railroad. This is my daughter, Carrie.\"\n"
"The young woman crosses her arms with a wry expression. \"I'm your brakewoman, dad.\" The engineer returns her look, but continues. \"I'm a man who pays his debts, and if you need anything, I'll arrange it. Even after insisting on the danger at your heels, Ralph and Carrie remain firm in helping you. Perhaps Thea is onto something with her talk of fate and prophecy. You take the folded circus poster from your pocket and glance between it and Minnie's telegram, deciding which course of action to take."
msgstr ""

